    "message": {
     "content": "This is a **phenomenal outcome**. Securing a **$200,000 sign-on bonus** at Google L6 alongside a base increase to $240,000 is near the top of what Google's compensation committee will approve. \n\nYour initial negotiation completely transformed this offer from mediocre to exceptionally strong.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Numbers Breakdown\n\n#### Year 1 Total Compensation\n\n| Component | Meta (Current) | Google (Revised Offer) | Difference |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Base Salary** | $240,000 | $240,000 | $0 |\n| **Target Bonus** | $36,000 (15%) | $48,000 (20%) | +$12,000 |\n| **Sign-on Bonus** | $0 | **$200,000** | +$200,000 |\n| **Equity (Year 1)** | ~$200,000 \u2013 $250,000 | **$270,000** *(flat)* to **$356,400** *(33% front-load)* | +$20,000 to +$106,400 |\n| **Year 1 Total** | **~$526,000** | **~$758,000 \u2013 $844,400** | **+$232,000 to +$318,400 (+44% to +60%)** |\n\n#### Multi-Year Reality Check\n* **Year 1:** You get a massive cash pop ($200k cash upfront completely eliminates the risk of leaving your unvested Meta RSUs).\n* **Year 2:** Expect **~$620,000 \u2013 $690,000** (Base + Bonus + Year 2 new-hire equity + Year 1 refresh).\n* **Years 3\u20134 (The Plateau):** Once the sign-on bonus is gone and the initial grant matures or drops (if front-loaded), compensation settles into the **$540,000 \u2013 $600,000** range depending on your performance ratings and refresh multipliers.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Should You Take It? (Decision Matrix)\n\nBecause the money is now definitively solved for the immediate 1\u20132 year window, this decision hinges on your **career strategy and culture preference**:\n\n#### Take Google If:\n1. **You want the upfront cash / derisked upside:** A guaranteed $200k cash sign-on in hand is better than waiting on unvested equity subject to stock price fluctuations.\n2. **You want Google on your resume:** Having both Meta (IC6) and Google (L6) at the senior level creates an elite, durable brand for future leadership/VP-track exits.\n3. **You want a change of pace/scope:** Google\u2019s culture tends to be more consensus-driven and cross-functional compared to Meta\u2019s fast-paced, high-pressure execution model. If you want to experience building at Google scale with slightly better work-life balance dynamics on average, this is the time.\n\n#### Stay at Meta If:\n1. **You value momentum and internal capital:** You are already established, trusted, and happy at Meta. Starting at a new company resets your network, institutional trust, and puts you into an onboarding ramp.\n2. **You are gunning for IC7 (Director track) soon:** If you are within 12\u201318 months of an IC7 promotion at Meta, leaving will delay that trajectory by at least 2\u20133 years at Google.\n3. **You believe Meta's refresh stacking will outpace Google long-term:** Meta historically rewards top-box performers (EE/GE) with aggressive equity refreshes that can beat Google\u2019s steady-state comp by Year 3 and Year 4.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Final Checklist Before Signing\n\nIf you decide to accept, make sure to confirm these two details in writing:\n\n1. **Sign-on Bonus Clawback Terms:** Confirm it is a standard 1-year prorated clawback (i.e., if you leave before 12 months, you only repay the remaining prorated portion, and after 12 months you owe $0).\n2. **Equity Schedule:** Verify whether the $1,080,000 grant vests **monthly/quarterly** and whether it follows the front-loaded (33/33/22/12) or flat (25/25/25/25) schedule so you can plan your tax strategy accordingly.",
